Generated clients: text derived from Apache-2.0 inputs
------------------------------------------------------

The files under `src/*/generated/*/` are written by the generators of
tools/build/proto-codegen (see docs/design/generated_sources.md). Each file's
first lines name its generator and, where the generator pins them, the
sha256 of each input. Not every generated library derives from third-party
input: those generated from komira's own `.proto` files and models (for
example komira_plan_proto, and records_db in komira_db_sqlite) are komira's
own text. The inputs
themselves are not committed here; the archives are pinned by sha256 and
fetched at build time.

1. AWS clients (`komira_aws_*`). Generated from the AWS service models
   (`service-2.json`) and endpoint rulesets of botocore, pinned in
   third_party/botocore/BUCK (version and archive sha256 there). botocore is
   licensed under the Apache License, Version 2.0, and its NOTICE reads:

       Botocore
       Copyright 2012-2022 Amazon.com, Inc. or its affiliates. All Rights Reserved.

   (The rest of botocore's NOTICE concerns the vendorized parts of the
   `requests` and `urllib3` libraries and a bundle of CA root certificates
   inside botocore's Python code and data; none of that is read or
   reproduced here.) botocore's LICENSE.txt and NOTICE are extracted
   unmodified from the archive as `//third_party/botocore:files[LICENSE.txt]`
   and `[NOTICE]`.

2. Google Cloud clients (`komira_gcp_*`) and the modules of their googleapis
   protos. Generated from the `.proto` files of
   https://github.com/googleapis/googleapis (Apache License, Version 2.0; it
   ships no NOTICE), at the commit pinned in tools/vendor/googleapis/BUCK.
   The archive's LICENSE is extracted unmodified as
   `//tools/vendor/googleapis:googleapis[LICENSE]`. The copyright holder
   is Google LLC: the headers of the pinned protos read "Copyright <year>
   Google LLC" and the Apache-2.0 notice (checked on google/type/expr.proto,
   google/iam/v1/iam_policy.proto and
   google/cloud/secretmanager/v1/service.proto). The generated Mojo does not
   carry that header; this entry is where the attribution is.

